; Your data in @VARDIR@ (asked, default No; a base Uninstall has asked already and
; answers by Set upvardelete). Without an UP-Term: assign there is no such drawer: it is
; not even looked at (EXISTS UP-Term:... would ask for the volume), and the data of a
; stand-alone program is in ENVARC:, which stays.
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If NOT WARN
  ; @include dist/common/uninstall-var.dos
  If NOT "$upkeepvar" EQ "YES"
; @include dist/common/resolve-uptreal.dos
    Delete >NIL: "@VARDIRREAL@" ALL QUIET
    Assign >NIL: UPTREAL:
  Else
    If EXISTS "@VARDIR@"
      Echo "Your data stayed in @VARDIR@."
    EndIf
  EndIf
  UnSet upkeepvar
EndIf
